{{was wotd|2009|October|30}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|morbidus||diseased|lang=la}}, from {{term|morbus||sickness|lang=la}}, itself from the root of {{term|morior||die|lang=la}} or directly from {{proto|Indo-European|mor-|to rub, pound, wear away|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɔː.bɪd/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɔɹ.bɪd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-morbid.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{originally}} Of, or relating to [[disease]].
# [[unhealthy|Unhealthy]] or [[unwholesome]], especially [[psychologically]]: mentally [[sick]] ([[sickly|ly]])
# Suggesting the [[horror]] of [[death]]; [[macabre]] or [[ghoulish]]
# [[grisly|Grisly]] or [[gruesome]].

====Derived terms====
* [[morbidity]]
* [[morbidly]]
* [[morbidness]]

====Related terms====
